    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 73\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 2127, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the social services law, in relation to school-\n      based health centers for purposes of managed care  programs  under\n      medicaid\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  provides that school based health centers (SBHCs) may seek\nand receive payment for  the  provision  of  medical  assistance  either\ndirectly  from  the  state  (fee  for  service),  or from a managed care\nprovider, even if the student is covered under a particular managed care\nprovider. In such cases reimbursement for SBHCs sponsored  by  Federally\nQualified  Health  Centers  (FQHCs)  shall  be at the federally mandated\nrate, and non-FQHC sponsored SBHCs at the ambulatory patient group (APG)\nrates. The bill also requires the SBHC and  managed  care  organizations\n(MCO) to enter into a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) developed by the\nDepartment  of  Health  for the purpose of coordinating care and quality\ninitiatives.\n \n  While I support the  efforts  of  care  coordination,  especially  for\nschool  aged  children,  this  legislation  as  drafted could jeopardize\nsignificant amounts of federal funding and  raises  additional  concerns\nregarding  state  program  administration and implementation. I am fully\nsupportive of SBHCs and the services they provide to  children,  and  am\ncommitted  to  ensuring  they are able to successfully provide services.\nHowever, this bill if signed could jeopardize significant federal  fund-\ning,  and must be done in the context of the budget after further review\nby the Department of Health and the Medicaid Program. Multiple  attempts\nto modify the bill to preserve federal funding were unsuccessful. There-\nfore, for these reasons, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
